1. Authorisation schemes must be predicated on criteria that preclude the competent authorities from exercising their powers in an arbitrary manner.  
2. The aforementioned criteria shall be:  
(a) non-discriminatory;  
(b) justified by overriding considerations of public interest;  
(c) proportionate to such objectives;  
(d) clear and unambiguous;  
(e) objective;  
(f) made public prior to implementation;  
(g) transparent and accessible.  

